  "bg_jurisdiction_assignment_method": "Dominant BG assignment: eb_jurisdiction_id / eb_jurisdiction_type columns already present on the promoted block-group parquet, produced by src/crimerisk/allocation.py::_dominant_bg_jurisdiction (highest allocation_share per BG from state/geometry/block_group_to_jurisdiction_crosswalk.parquet). This is the same dominant-jurisdiction assignment the allocator uses elsewhere in the pipeline (e.g. for the EB jurisdiction prior). For each city, predicted_share is expected_count_<offense> for every BG with eb_jurisdiction_id == the city's jurisdiction_id, normalized to sum to 1 within that BG set. Cross-checked against the raw crosswalk allocation_share for exclusivity (see sanity_checks).",
  "scoring_protocol": {
    "metric_name": "incident_weighted_tvd",
    "definition": "Per (city, offense): TVD = 0.5 * sum_over_BG(|predicted_share - truth_share|), where truth_share is the onboarded incident-count share by BG (same BG universe as predicted_share, both normalized to sum to 1 by scripts/diagnostics/nested_city_cv_harness.py::_normalize_share). Aggregated across cities per offense as the incident-count-weighted mean (scripts/diagnostics/nested_city_cv_harness.py::_weighted_mean applied to the tvd column with incident_total weights, i.e. the tvd_incident_weighted_mean field produced by _summarize_group).",
    "function_module_path": "scripts/diagnostics/nested_city_cv_harness.py:_score_variant (per-city-offense TVD), :_weighted_mean + :_summarize_group (incident-weighted aggregation)",
    "identical_to_nested_cv": true,
    "bg_universe": "Same BG set as predicted_share (city's eb_jurisdiction_id-assigned block groups); truth incidents falling outside this BG set after geocoding must be documented, not silently dropped."
